    "diagnosis": "Schematic representation of traditional serrated adenoma (TSA) progression in the serrated neoplasia pathway",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "TSAs may develop de novo or possibly (dotted line) from a sessile serrated lesion (SSL) or a hyperplastic polyp (HP). TSAs progress via the <em>BRAF</em> or <em>KRAS</em> pathway to high-grade dysplasia and mismatch repair (MMR)-proficient carcinomas. WNT pathway activation occurs early in TSA development through either RNF43 mutation in <em>BRAF</em>-mutated TSAs or RSPO fusions in <em>KRAS</em>-mutated TSAs. Progression to high-grade dysplasia and carcinoma involves <em>TP53</em> mutation and, for <em>BRAF</em>-mutated TSAs, p16 loss.",
